            <div xml:id="d52-a1">

                <pb facs="0119" n="57" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg57"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 16.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Goodloe to Count
                            Aspremont Lynden.</hi></head>
                <p>Monsieur <hi rendition="#small-caps">Le Compte</hi>: In surrendering the duties
                    of minister for foreign affairs to resume those of senator, I beg you to believe
                    that you carry with you my sincerest wishes for your happiness and
                    prosperity.</p>
                <p>Our official acquaintance, though of short duration, was sufficient to enable me
                    to form a high appreciation of your many accomplishments, perfect courtesy, and
                    undeviating kindness, and I trust that our future personal relations may
                    continue to be of a like pleasant and agreeable nature.</p>
                <p>I pray, Monsieur Le Compte, that you accept the assurances of my most
                    distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. CASSIUS GOODLOE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Monsieur <hi rendition="#small-caps">Le Compte d’Aspremont Lynden.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
